# Super Dodge Ball (USA) — "throw at everyone" input schedule.
#
# Drives the stock game through team-select into a match, then holds B to throw.
# Controls (NES): B throws, A passes, A+B jumps. Pressing B without the ball is
# a catch attempt, so holding it is harmless when the CPU has possession.
#
# This is the stress vector for the character-flicker mod, not a flicker
# reproduction: a scripted idle run never reaches the game states that break the
# mod's sprite-list bookkeeping (docs/research.md section 2.1). Throwing gets
# players hit, which is what exposed the runaway capture list -- the symptom is
# the court filling with copies of itself in a trail.
#
# Run it with SDB_TRACE=1 and read the peak-list column; a healthy frame is tens
# of sprites. Per-frame present-out at this length is ~1.5 GB, so trace without
# --present-out unless you want the pictures:
#
#   SDB_TRACE=1 ./build-cycle/nes_game "roms/Super Dodge Ball (USA).nes" \
#     --frames 8000 --input tas/vectors/sdb_throw.input --ram-init zeros \
#     --mods-root build-cycle/mods
#
# Format: one "<frame> <BUTTONS>" line per state change, absolute state
# ("-" is release). `#` starts a comment.
#
# Up to frame 440 is sdb_idle.input: title -> team-select -> match. After that,
# B for 12 frames, released for 12, so every throw needs a fresh press edge.
